00:21:00,238 --> 00:21:06,624
So given a stack trace from CPings, the setfix system would use a bunch of strategies.

163
00:21:06,864 --> 00:21:09,636
Let's say here we are talking about four.

164
00:21:10,414 --> 00:21:13,900
For high-firing crash, it may simply revert the full diff.

165
00:21:14,864 --> 00:21:21,732
And if there is a potential merge conflict, that may trigger the second strategy, we may revert partial div.

166
00:21:22,304 --> 00:21:24,944
And the third one is template-based fixing.

167
00:21:25,104 --> 00:21:35,204
This is more about forward fixing by following the previous fixed patterns from developers, and that would generate a template-based fix.

168
00:21:36,046 --> 00:21:46,532
For cases we don't have historical knowledge or it needs a final ground fix, we may mutate across abstract syntax tree for a final ground fix.

169
00:21:47,246 --> 00:21:53,316
So this process may generate many fixed candidates, so we need to evaluate how valid they are.

170
00:21:54,958 --> 00:22:03,104
For the fixed validation workflow, we let the system ask a bunch of questions and execute to answer them.

171
00:22:03,344 --> 00:22:07,364
First one, we build app to check if any compilation errors.

172
00:22:07,918 --> 00:22:13,700
And the second, we rerun sapings to check whether the crash can be reproduced or not.

